==========================================================================
Section 1 — Redaction (clipboard content never reaches the UI surface)
==========================================================================

Unit assertions (xcodebuild output, verbatim):

Test Case '-[BicTermTests.HerdrClipboardTests testEchoNeverContainsClipboardContent]' passed (0.069 seconds).
Test Case '-[BicTermTests.HerdrClipboardTests testMultilinePasteWritesGoldenFrameByteExact]' passed (0.045 seconds).
Test Case '-[BicTermTests.HerdrClipboardTests testNonASCIIPasteWritesGoldenFrame]' passed (0.045 seconds).
Test Case '-[BicTermTests.HerdrClipboardTests testOversizePasteRejectedBeforeTheFFI]' passed (0.034 seconds).

The echo surface (herdr-input-echo / debugInputEcho) carries only:
  paste(NB->pane)            — text paste, byte count + destination
  image(NB.ext->pane)        — image send, byte count + extension + destination
  remoteClipboard(NB)        — server clipboard arrival, byte count
  copyRemote(NB)             — explicit copy gesture, byte count
  autoCopyRemote(NB)         — per-host opt-in applied, byte count
  clipboardDropped           — oversize / malformed server frame dropped
  pasteTooLarge              — text over the 1 MiB cap, no frame sent
  pasteTargetChanged         — pane / boot changed between read and send
  frozen / offline / writeFailed — typed notes
The strings pasted into the app, the base64 server payload, and the
decoded remote text are NEVER added to the echo array, NEVER logged via
os_log / NSLog at any point, and NEVER stored on HerdrEndpointState.

testOversizePasteRejectedBeforeTheFFI proves the 1 MiB cap (text) gates
before the FFI is touched, so oversized pasted text never crosses the wire.

==========================================================================
Section 2 — Zero automatic reads (pasteboard stats line, unit + UI)
==========================================================================

HerdrPasteboard (DEBUG-only counters, @MainActor):
   readCount  — incremented only inside readText() / readImageData(),
                 both called exclusively from beginPaste() — i.e. only
                 from a user gesture (UIPasteControl tap / cmd+v).
   writeCount — incremented only inside writeText(), called from
                 copyRemoteClipboardToPasteboard / setAutoCopyRemoteClipboard.
   lastWrittenText — debug-only record for the unit binding round trip.

UI assertions (xcodebuild output, verbatim):

Test Case '-[BicTermUITests.HerdrClipboardUITests testRemoteClipboardCopyGestureWritesOnExplicitCopy]' passed (8.813 seconds).
   statsText() == "pasteboard r:0 w:0"  — before the Copy tap
   after tap: "pasteboard r:0 w:1"       — exactly one write, zero reads
   echo assertion: contains("copyRemote(27B)")
   echo does NOT contain "hello remote"  — byte counts only, never content

Test Case '-[BicTermUITests.HerdrClipboardUITests testAutoCopyOptInWritesOnArrival]' passed (8.628 seconds).
   banner surfaces (remote arrived, not silently written)
   statsText() == "pasteboard r:0 w:0"  — default OFF confirmed
   after "Always for This Host" tap: echo autoCopyRemote(27B), stats "r:0 w:1"

The UIPasteControl XCUI tap path is not exercised on the iOS 18 simulator
this task targets (a known XCUI delivery limitation; see file header in
HerdrClipboardUITests.swift). Gesture-level coverage of the read-once
contract lives in the unit suite: testEmptyPasteIsSilent (no read on
empty / null), testMalformedClipboardFrameDropsNonFatally (server-side
drop, no client read), and the paste-vector tests (every paste path goes
through enqueueInput -> applyInputEvent -> client.sendPaste, and the model
records the byte-count echo only).

